            <ArticleTitle>Finding host targets for HIV therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>175-176</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/ng.3777</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A CRISPR screen conducted in a CD4+ T cell leukemia line has identified host factors required for HIV infection but dispensable for cellular survival. The results highlight sulfation on the HIV co-receptor CCR5 and cellular aggregation as potential targets for therapeutic intervention.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
